/-
# HC Gap L4 -- FRONT C13: E6 case derivation skeleton (R502).

The paper's E6 case (Section 5 + rem:E6-V27-vacuity) states: if the
Mumford-Tate group of X has an E6(-14) simple factor on MT^der(H^3),
then HC(X) holds. The proof uses:

1. The alpha_s string structure of E6 representations
2. The Grothendieck-Chern algebraicity argument
3. The weight-parity constraint forcing every E6-invariant Hodge
   class to be algebraic

This file constructs the STRUCTURED derivation skeleton for the E6 case.

All R502 substantive declarations kernel-pure.
-/

import HodgeReduction.HCGapL4.FrontC12_ClassicalCartanDerivation
